<title>POLAND: POLAND RAISES MIN PRICE OF 5-YR BOND TO 81.10.</title>
<headline>POLAND RAISES MIN PRICE OF 5-YR BOND TO 81.10.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland raised the minimum price of its 12-percent 5-year bonds, maturing June 12, 2001, to 81.10 from 80.76 at the last tender and the average price rose to 81.34 from 80.87, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>It said it sold 191 million zlotys worth of the bonds after investors bid to buy 406 million against a 300 million zloty offer.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
